cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Abliteration Lens in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Abliteration Lens: a mixing desk for a language model's forward pass"
abstract: >-
  A local instrument that changes how an open-weight language model's
  forward pass runs while it writes, as a chain of strips on a desk, and sets the diverged text
  beside the text the unchanged model writes from the same prompt and seed. The first host of
  Vector Abliteration Units (VAU). Part of the Vector Lab family of research instruments.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Berry
    given-names: David M.
    affiliation: University of Sussex
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7737-5586"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vector-lab-tools/abliteration-lens"
url: "https://vector-lab-tools.github.io/abliteration-lens/"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.1.19
date-released: 2026-11-27
keywords:
  - language models
  - interpretability
  - steering
  - abliteration
  - Vector Abliteration Units
